A true primitive must satisfy **four criteria**:

### 1️⃣ Atomic
✔ Cannot be meaningfully subdivided
An SEU represents one experiential surface — no partial execution possible.

### 2️⃣ Composable
✔ Can be combined into higher-order constructs
Multiple SEUs compose:

* Orchestration Units (OUs)
* Portfolios
* Programs
* Enterprise-level experience strategy

### 3️⃣ Semantically Stable
✔ Means the same thing across contexts
An SEU’s identity does not drift across:

* time
* channels
* teams
* models
* LLMs

“Delayed Lab Results” means the same thing everywhere — forever.

### 4️⃣ Operationally Complete
✔ Sufficient to execute work
An SEU contains everything required to:

* prioritize
* route
* act
* measure outcomes
* remember results

No reinterpretation layer required.

👉 **Only SEU satisfies all four. Nothing else in CX does.**

